import java.util.Scanner;

public class PrimeNumber {

   public static void main(String[] args) {

      Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
      System.out.print("Enter a number: ");
      int num = sc.nextInt();

      boolean prime = true;

      //checking if the number is divisible by any other number except 1 and itself
      for(int i = 2; i < num; i++) {
         if(num % i == 0) {
            prime = false;
            break;
         }
      }

      if(prime) {
         System.out.println("The given number " + num + " is a Prime number");
      } else {
         System.out.println("The given number " + num + " is NOT a Prime number.");
      }
   }

}

Explanation:

We take input using a Scanner object and store it in the variable num.

We initialize a boolean variable prime to true, assuming initially that the number is prime.

We use a for loop to check all numbers from 2 to num - 1 to see if the number is divisible by any of them. If it is, we set the prime variable to false and break out of the loop.

If prime is still true after the loop, we print that the given number is a prime number. Otherwise, we print that it is not a prime number.

Note: A number is considered prime if it is only divisible by 1 and itself.

