There are several ways to convert an int array to a string in C#. Here are a few examples:

1. Using the ToString() method:

int[] numbers = { 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 };
string strNumbers = string.Join(",", numbers.Select(n => n.ToString()).ToArray());

This will convert the integer array to a comma-separated string of numbers.

2. Using the string.Join() method:

int[] numbers = { 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 };
string strNumbers = string.Join(",", numbers);

This will also convert the integer array to a comma-separated string of numbers.

3. Using a loop:

int[] numbers = { 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 };
string strNumbers = "";
for (int i = 0; i < numbers.Length; i++)
{
    strNumbers += numbers[i].ToString();
    if (i < numbers.Length - 1)
    {
        strNumbers += ",";
    }
}

This will loop through the integer array and build a string of numbers separated by commas.

Note: These examples assume that the goal is to convert an array of integers to a string representation. If the goal is to convert an array of characters (such as ASCII codes) to a string, the same methods can be used but without the .ToString() call on each element.

