Defining and Exporting Modules

To define a module in TypeScript, you can simply create a new file and put your code in it. By default, every TypeScript file is considered a module, and variables and functions defined in it are local to that module scope. To make a variable or function available to other modules, you need to explicitly export it using the `export` keyword. For example:

```typescript
// user.ts
export interface User {
  id: number;
  name: string;
}

// main.ts
